<title>UK: Britain's PIA reduces size of board.</title>
<headline>Britain's PIA reduces size of board.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Personal Investment Authority (PIA) which regulates the sale of pensions and other investments to the public, said on Wednesday it was reducing the size of its board from 21 to 17 directors.</p>
<p>The reduction will take place at the PIA's next annual meeting when four directors conclude their term of office.</p>
<p>The directors concerned are Sir John Bailey, Lawrence Churchill, Allan Daffern and Sir Leonard Peach.</p>
<p>The decision reflects the PIA's long standing commitment to reduce the size of its board, it said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
